### Description

Update the specified job plan: its name, the enabled steps and the global variable values.

This API operates on the **current step snapshot of the job plan** and does not require the plan to be in sync with
its job template. After the template changes (the plan's `need_update` becomes `true`), the plan can still be
updated directly; only enabling a step newly added to the template requires calling `sync_job_plan` first.

Prerequisites: the job plan exists in the scope; the caller has permission to edit it. Plan names must be unique
within the same resource scope and job template.

### Request Parameters

#### Body Parameters

| Field         | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                                                 |
|---------------|--------|----------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| bk_scope_type | string | Yes      | Resource scope type. Allowed values: `biz` (business), `biz_set` (business set)                                                             |
| bk_scope_id   | string | Yes      | Resource scope ID matching `bk_scope_type` (business ID or business set ID)                                                                 |
| job_plan_id   | long   | Yes      | Job plan ID; must be greater than 0; the plan must exist                                                                                    |
| name          | string | Yes      | Job plan name, 1–60 characters; must not contain HTML special characters `<`, `>`, `"`, `'`; must be unique within the same scope and template |
| enable_steps  | array  | Yes      | **Plan step** IDs to enable; an empty array is not allowed; steps not listed are disabled; every ID must belong to the plan                 |
| variables     | array  | No       | Overrides for template global variables, matched by variable name; fails if the name is unknown or the value type does not match the template; variable names must be unique in one request |

The IDs in `enable_steps` are **plan step IDs**, which differ from the template step IDs used by `create_job_plan`;
they can be read via the v3 API `get_job_plan_detail`. An ID that does not belong to the plan results in an error; to
enable a step newly added to the job template, call `sync_job_plan` first.

The field is mandatory to prevent accidental clearing: the server disables every step that is not listed, so a
missing field would be equivalent to disabling all steps of the plan.

##### variables[] element

| Field           | Type    | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |
|-----------------|---------|----------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| name            | string  | Yes      | Global variable name in the template, matched by name (not by variable ID); must be non-blank                                                                                                                                |
| value           | string  | No       | Default variable value for string, namespace, ciphertext, associative array, index array, or execute account types in the template; execute account value is the account ID string; ignored when `follow_template` is `true` |
| execute_target  | object  | No       | Execute targets; only when the template variable is an execute-target list and `follow_template` is `false`; must not be used together with `value`                                                                          |
| follow_template | boolean | No       | Whether to keep the template default. Allowed values: `true` (use template default), `false` (use `value` or `execute_target` from this request; default `false`). When `true`, `execute_target` must not be provided        |

